{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Happy are you, O Israel.</b> And then you will attain the happiness that is the highest possible rank for a nation." "<b>Who is like you.</b> To the point that no nation like you will be found, as it says: וְאִשְּׁרוּ אֶתְכֶם כָּל הַגּוֹיִם (Malachi 3:12)." "<b>A people saved by HaShem.</b> So that your salvation will not come through your own warring, but HaShem will fight for you." "<b>The shield of your help.</b> He it is who helped you at the time of the destruction, so that you were not annihilated, as it says (Psalms 124:2–8): לוּלֵי ה׳ שֶׁהָיָה לָנוּ, אֲזַי הַמַּיִם שְׁטָפוּנוּ, עֶזְרֵנוּ בְּשֵׁם ה׳." "<b>And who is the sword of your pride.</b> And He it is who will be the sword of your pride, so that you are exalted over the nations through your warring against them, as it says: כִּי בָאֵשׁ ה׳ נִשְׁפָּט וּבְחַרְבּוֹ אֶת כָּל בָּשָׂר (Isaiah 66:16)." "<b>And your enemies will come cringing to you.</b> They who formerly despised you will deny themselves when they come to honor you, as it says: וְהִשְׁתַּחֲווּ עַל כַּפּוֹת רַגְלַיִךְ כָּל מְנַאֲצָיִךְ (Isaiah 60:14)." "<b>And you shall tread upon their high places.</b> For even their kings will be submissive to you, as it says (Isaiah 49:23): וְהָיוּ מְלָכִים אֹמְנַיִךְ וגו׳, אַפַּיִם אַרְצָה יִשְׁתַּחֲווּ לָךְ."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:47.288931830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}